1. Insertion at the Beginning
Before: [20, 30, 40]
Insert 10
After : [10, 20, 30, 40]
All existing elements are shifted one position to the right.

2. Insertion at a Specific Position (Middle)
Before: [10, 20, 40]
Insert 30 at index 2
After : [10, 20, 30, 40]
Elements from that position onward are shifted right.

3. Insertion at the End
Before: [10, 20, 30]
Insert 40
After : [10, 20, 30, 40]
No shifting required (if space is available).
Time Complexity: O(1)

So, in Data Structures, array insertion is generally classified into 3 types:

Insertion at the beginning
Insertion at a specific position (middle)
Insertion at the end
